The works this plugin shows, their images and their data belong to the
museums below and are not covered by this plugin's licence. The plugin asks
only for works each museum marks as free to use, and always shows, with the
work, its title, artist and date, the museum and the licence (or the credit
line the museum's terms give). It uses no museum's logo, and Kiosko and this
plugin are not affiliated with, nor endorsed by, any of them.

The Metropolitan Museum of Art, New York
  Collection API, https://collectionapi.metmuseum.org (no key).
  Open Access data is published under Creative Commons Zero (CC0); images of
  works in the public domain (`isPublicDomain`) are free for any use.
  https://metmuseum.github.io/  https://www.metmuseum.org/hubs/open-access
  Shown as: "The Met · Public domain".

Art Institute of Chicago
  API, https://api.artic.edu, and IIIF images, https://www.artic.edu/iiif/2
  (no key). Data CC0 except the `description` field (CC BY 4.0), which this
  plugin does not use. Images of public-domain works (`is_public_domain`)
  are CC0 ("CC0 Public Domain Designation"), under the Terms and Conditions
  of artic.edu. Requests carry an `AIC-User-Agent` header, as its docs ask.
  https://api.artic.edu/docs/  https://www.artic.edu/image-licensing
  https://www.artic.edu/terms
  Shown as: "Art Institute of Chicago · CC0".

Rijksmuseum, Amsterdam
  Data services, https://data.rijksmuseum.nl (search, EDM records) and IIIF
  images, https://iiif.micr.io (no key). Only images under the Public Domain
  Mark 1.0 or CC0 1.0 (`edmRights`) are shown. Its Information and Data
  Policy allows free use and kindly asks to credit the Rijksmuseum.
  https://data.rijksmuseum.nl/policy/
  Shown as: "Rijksmuseum · Public domain" (or "· CC0").

National Palace Museum (國立故宮博物院), Taipei
  Open data, https://digitalarchive.npm.gov.tw/opendata/ (search and IIIF
  manifests) and IIIF images, https://iiifod.npm.gov.tw (no key). Its open
  data statement: images up to 1 megapixel are dedicated to the public domain
  (CC0); images up to 6 megapixels and the site's texts are under CC BY 4.0,
  free to use without application, for any purpose, free of charge, with
  the attribution "<title> The National Palace Museum, Taipei, CC BY 4.0 @
  www.npm.gov.tw" (or "<title> 國立故宮博物院，臺北，CC BY 4.0 @
  www.npm.gov.tw"). This plugin asks for images of at most 1 megapixel,
  shows paintings from before 1912 only, and shows that attribution with the
  title.
  Shown as: "The National Palace Museum, Taipei, CC BY 4.0 @ www.npm.gov.tw"
  (in Chinese for Chinese readers).

The test fixtures in src/fixtures are answers of these APIs saved on 26
November 2026 (JSON, and one trimmed HTML page of the National Palace
Museum's search), under the licences above; they contain no images. The
screenshots in docs/ show Gustave Caillebotte, "Paris Street; Rainy Day",
1877, Art Institute of Chicago, CC0. The demo picture ("Hills at dawn") is
drawn by the plugin.
